<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luang Prabang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Luang Phrabang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luang Prabang is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, the early royal capital of Lan Xang and later the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Kingdom of Luang Phrabang</a>, formed when Lan Xang split in 1707. Under French rule from 1893 its kings kept their thrones as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. In 1946 the Lao lands were united under the king of Luang Phrabang as the Kingdom of Laos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luang-prabang.jpg" alt="Luang Prabang" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 松岡明芳 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phou_si_Luang_Prabang_Laos_%E3%83%97%E3%83%BC%E3%82%B7%E3%83%BC%E3%81%AE%E4%B8%98_%E3%83%A9%E3%82%AA%E3%82%B9%E3%83%BB%E3%83%AB%E3%82%A2%E3%83%B3%E3%83%97%E3%83%A9%E3%83%90%E3%83%BC%E3%83%B3_DSCF6777.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
